# runner-netprobe.service — the probe/auto-fence action itself. Triggered by
# runner-netprobe.timer every ~30 s; do NOT enable or start this unit directly,
# enable the TIMER (there is deliberately no [Install] section here).
#
# NO dependency on k3s-agent ON PURPOSE (contrast with runner-auto-leave.service,
# which orders itself after k3s-agent because its STOP must run while the kubelet
# is still alive): this probe must keep running EXACTLY when the agent/Cilium is
# broken or stopped — a dead data plane under a live control plane is the failure
# it exists to catch (2026-11-12: node Ready, API reachable, cilium_vxlan rx
# frozen at 0, CI frozen ~5 h). It needs no cluster-local anything: only the
# host network, to reach the API (10.2.248.31:6443) and probe the VIP.
#
# No User= on purpose (same as runner-auto-leave.service): the unit runs as root,
# which is what can read the node-ops kubeconfig under /root or /home/bruno and
# write /run/runner-netprobe. The systemd environment has neither HOME nor the
# Nix profile in PATH — runner-netprobe.sh therefore resolves its kubeconfig and
# kubectl explicitly, exactly like its sibling hook. Cluster-side permissions
# come from the git-managed node-ops ServiceAccount (kubernetes/arc/node-ops-rbac.yaml:
# nodes get/list/patch + pods get/list/delete — precisely cordon + pod deletion,
# nothing more), never from the local user.
[Unit]
Description=Auto-fence this CI runner node when the Cilium data plane dies (netprobe)
After=network-online.target
Wants=network-online.target

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=/usr/local/bin/runner-netprobe.sh
# Worst-case budget, from the code paths (each kubectl: --request-timeout=10s
# inside an outer `timeout 15`; each TCP probe `timeout 6`):
#   CP probe 6 + DP probe 6 + sleep 2 + node read 15 + cordon 15 + read-back 15
#   + enumerate 15 + delete 15 + post-delete re-check 15  =  ~119 s
# If a run outlives the 30 s timer interval, systemd simply skips that tick
# (a oneshot is never started twice) — cadence degrades, never duplicates.
TimeoutStartSec=150
